{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"7d4d974d-a68d-4476-947c-b0e713a107af","runId":"69d88ea4-94dc-4ee1-8be5-94e81414e7b0","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":11,"previousEventHash":"sha256:e7f799d51e4b9aa4f548fa2c1c2a4b87084a7b9e62951a34d4f6cf31b24eea46","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a03c73-a5c6-77c7-a622-ad858003aa20","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-26T05:10:01.104Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":["Allowed paths are exactly `test/fixtures/work-on-e2e-receipt.txt` and `test/smoke/work-on-e2e-receipt.test.ts`.","The fixture will be written with one trailing newline and no other bytes.","The smoke test will use node:fs/promises, node:path, node:test, and node:assert/strict; it will only read and assert.","No production source, policy, workflow, package metadata, or unrelated test files will change.","Verification is the configured `npm run check` command; the allowlist is empty, so GitHub CI remains parent-owned."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:PLANNER -->\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### Objective\nAdd the disposable deterministic work-on receipt fixture and a smoke test that asserts its exact contents.\n\n### Allowed Paths\n- `test/fixtures/work-on-e2e-receipt.txt`\n- `test/smoke/work-on-e2e-receipt.test.ts`\n\n### Forbidden Changes\n- No production source, policy, workflow, package metadata, or unrelated test changes.\n- No network access or writes from the smoke test.\n- No changes outside the two allowed paths.\n\n### Invariants\n- Fixture bytes are exactly `forgedock-work-on-e2e-v1\\n`.\n- Test reads the fixture relative to its own source location and asserts exact string equality.\n- Test remains deterministic and uses the repository's node:test runner.\n\n### Acceptance Mapping\n- AC1: create only the two allowed paths.\n- AC2: use a local read and strict equality assertion; no network or writes.\n- AC3: run `npm run check`.\n- AC4: leave production and metadata untouched.\n- AC5: retain dogfood as the PR target through ForgeDock.\n\n### Steps\n1. Create the fixture with the exact required contents.\n2. Create the smoke test using `node:test` and `node:assert/strict`.\n3. Run the named `npm run check` verification.\n4. Inspect the diff and commit only the two allowed files.\n\n<!-- PLAN:COMPLETE -->"}}
